      "writtenOn": "2026-06-05T23:16:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "[AI review] In the Gerrit diff API a chunk carries exactly one of `ab` (context), `a`/`b` (edit), or `skip` — they\u0027re mutually exclusive. The current code calls all four emitters unconditionally, so a malformed or future-format response with both `ab` and `skip` in the same chunk would double-count line numbers silently. A short comment asserting the invariant (or an early-return guard) would help future readers:\n\n```python\n# Gerrit chunks carry exactly one of: ab (context), a/b (edit), or skip.\n```",
      "revId": "f0b1a7a15b963de8b630cec57b9330dd837fea5f",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
