      "writtenOn": "2026-06-05T23:16:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "[AI review] `if count:` treats `0` and `None` the same way. A `{\"skip\": 0}` chunk (valid but degenerate) would silently skip the emit, which is harmless, but the line-number increment would also be skipped — same no-op, so no real bug today. Still, `if count is not None and count \u003e 0:` is more precise and makes the intent explicit.",
      "revId": "f0b1a7a15b963de8b630cec57b9330dd837fea5f",
